#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""MyBot UTXO metrics v4 — read-only V50/R12.9 dense-state indicators.

Internal build: utxo_metrics_v4-r5-v50-r12.9-lineage-prod.

This replaces the legacy DuckDB-UTXO metrics path.  Authoritative inputs:
  * V50 dense state: tx_records.bin, outputs.bin, closes.bin, checkpoint.bin/state.meta
  * canonical Stage blocks parquet: height -> block_time
  * daily BTC/USD price CSV
  * V51.5.4 core-chain guard evidence (required by default)

No AWS RAW parquet is used for canonical metrics.  No authoritative state is mutated.
The process holds the same three shared freeze locks as the independent V51 auditor.

Dense-state semantics (V50 R11/R12.9):
  TxRecord    <32sQIIII> = txid, first_out, height, tx_index, vout_count, flags
  OutputRecord<QqQII>    = tx_seq, value_sats, script_offset, script_len, flags
  CloseRecord <QQII>     = output_id, closer_tx_seq, vin, type
  close type=1: normal spend; type=2: BIP30 overwrite (not a spend/SOPR input)

Metric policy changes vs v3:
  * full history always starts at genesis; no partial-range cumsum mode;
  * raw input coverage comes from exact type=1 CloseRecords, not AWS parquet;
  * aSOPR removes outputs younger than 1 hour (3600 seconds), not 1 calendar day;
  * MVRV Z-score = (market_cap - realized_cap) / expanding_std(market_cap);
  * pre-price cost basis is explicitly 0 USD; price-dependent ratios remain NaN until valid;
  * BIP30 overwrite removes UTXO value/cost basis/HODL inventory but is excluded from spend metrics.

Outputs are atomic CSVs plus a provenance manifest in --output-dir.
"""
